            <ArticleTitle>Letter to the Editor regarding the article: &quot;identifying pre-hospital factors associated with outcome for major trauma patients in a regional trauma network: an exploratory study&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s13049-017-0454-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this Letter to the Editor was to report some methodological shortcomings in a recently published article. Issues regarding missing values and overfitting are mentioned. First, Complete Case (CC) analysis was used instead of an imputation method. Second, there was a high chance of overfitting and lack of model validation. In conclusion, the results of this study should be interpret with caution and further research is necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
